{
  "name": "Experts to debate quality in education at AKU-IED research and policy dialogue",
  "parent_id": 203313772661931,
  "group_id": "bc85f77e-98dc-4408-bcc7-94b82c3da52b",
  "alternates": [],
  "created_at": "2026-07-30T15:19:41.098Z",
  "deleted_at": null,
  "sort_by_date": null,
  "tag_list": [],
  "updated_at": "2026-08-12T15:02:25.497Z",
  "published_at": "2026-08-12T15:02:25.485Z",
  "id": 203715301813030,
  "uuid": "f035f0a9-2998-41eb-8a57-70ac705cc709",
  "is_folder": false,
  "content": {
    "_uid": "6d27ecaf-372e-1efc-b388-e6650ed838e5",
    "body": [
      {
        "_uid": "a71552e1-1b4b-3d1d-c0b4-add82a1e0f5d",
        "content": {
          "type": "doc",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Participants will include Khushnood Lashari, Secretary Education, Government of Punjab, representatives of federal and provincial governments, academic institutions and community, as well as policy think-tanks, NGOs, and researchers from both public and private sectors.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "The dialogue will explore and debate issues of quality across the education sector in Pakistan, with particular focus on quality at the different stages of schooling and the current system. Finally, it will also recommend steps towards achieving quality in the education system in the country.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "This programme concludes the series of five dialogues on key issues in education. Four policy dialogues on Teacher Education, Decentralisation in Education and Effective Resource Utilisation through Public-Private Partnership in Education, and Curriculum Reforms, were held earlier in Karachi, Islamabad, Quetta and Peshawar in 2002 and early 2003.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Aga Khan University is part of Aga Khan Development Network, a group of private international development agencies, founded by His Highness the Aga Khan, which work in the developing countries of Asia and Africa.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
